# The committed build is bytes, not text.
#
# web/dist is in git — that is the whole reason `npm start` needs no bundler —
# and vite names every chunk by a hash of its CONTENT. With line-ending
# normalisation on, a rebuild on a checkout where core.autocrlf is true
# produces a different hash for the same source than a rebuild on one where it
# is not, so the directory grew a second copy of all 22 chunks and index.html
# named only one set. Forty-four files where twenty-two are reachable, and
# nothing to tell you which half is dead.
#
# -text turns normalisation off for everything under it: what vite wrote is
# what git stores and what the next checkout gets, whatever anyone's
# core.autocrlf says.
web/dist/** -text

# The shell scripts the deployment runs on a Linux host. A CRLF shebang line
# is `/usr/bin/env bash\r`, which is not a program, and the error names a file
# that plainly exists.
*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/gc text eol=lf
docker/Caddyfile text eol=lf
